  "historical_basis": "An original, interpretive Republican Roman civic district around 270 BCE. Streets, masonry, courtyard housing and roofed civic space evoke the period; this is not an archaeological reconstruction or a survey of all Rome. The muster house is a gameplay abstraction for the garrison, not an assertion that a later imperial permanent barracks existed here. The curia represents civic administration rather than a claim about an exact surviving plan. The tavern represents a modest food and wine shop; later imperial monuments are deliberately absent.",
